SUMMARY:Deer New Jersey\, Let’s Find Balance for Our Forests\, Farms and Families
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a timely conversation about one of New Jersey’s most pressing wildlife challenges. Joe Basralian\, Project Coordinator of Deer New Jersey\, will highlight the crisis unfolding in areas where deer herd densities have reached critical highs\, and share opportunities for our community to get involved in responsible\, ethical deer stewardship. \nDeer New Jersey’s mission is to achieve natural balance across our state by supporting a deer stewardship movement for the people\, wildlife\, and land we love. Their vision: a future where New Jersey’s land\, wildlife\, and communities thrive\, stewarded by all of us working together toward solutions that align with both biological and cultural goals. Come learn more\, ask questions\, and discover how you can be part of the solution. \nThis event is available in WEBINAR and IN-PERSON formats\, please be sure to select the correct ticket type and check out with your preferred email for the zoom link if selecting webinar. \nAbout the Speaker: Basralian\, who grew up in Franklin Lakes\, has spent 25 years working in the financial industry and 8 years in environmental conservation full-time\, often uniting diverse parties to achieve common goals. He is a 2026 appointee to the NJ Highlands Council and the Great Swamp Watershed Association board. He participates in many volunteer causes\, including the NJ League of Conservation Voters\, whose board he served on for nine years. He’s a graduate of NYU’s Stern School of Business and Cornell University and lives in Chatham Township. \nCOST: FREE \nCANCELLATION: NJ Audubon’s programs require a minimum number of registrants to run. If we cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, all participants will be notified as soon as possible and are eligible for a full refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 48 hours in advance. Sorry\, no refund for cancellations less than 48 hours in advance unless due to health emergencies; however\, registrations can be transferred to another program in the future. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/deer-new-jersey-lets-find-balance-for-our-forests-farms-and-families/
LOCATION:Lorrimer Sanctuary\, 790 Ewing Avenue\, Franklin Lakes\, NJ\, 07417\, United States
CATEGORIES:Lorrimer Sanctuary,Webinar,Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Deer-New-Jersey-Lets-Find-Balance-for-Our-Forests-Farms-and-Families.webp
